WEBVTT

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.448
-(distant roar)
-(all gasp)

00:00:21.996 --> 00:00:22.997
Uh...

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.040
Hello?

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.083
(echoing)

00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:27.209
(roars)

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.294
(screams)

00:00:30.504 --> 00:00:31.881
(growling)

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:38.971
(screams)

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.306
(gasps)

00:00:41.682 --> 00:00:43.017
(grunts) Yeah!

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.144
Oh! Hello, mammals.

00:00:45.561 --> 00:00:46.729
Hi, Buck!

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:48.314
Hi. (screaming)

00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:49.648
Bye, Buck!

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:51.567
BUCK: Um, a little help.

00:00:52.026 --> 00:00:53.027
(grunting)

00:00:53.903 --> 00:00:54.904
(screaming)

00:00:55.821 --> 00:00:58.449
(groaning)

00:00:58.532 --> 00:01:00.451
Right on the spleen!

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.786
Utterly useless, but totally hurts.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.414
(laughs) Hey, Buck. Welcome back, buddy.

00:01:05.497 --> 00:01:08.417
Wait. This half-a-snack
is the dinosaur whisperer?

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.794
And expert salsa dancer.

00:01:10.878 --> 00:01:12.922
-(singing)
-(salsa music playing)

00:01:13.923 --> 00:01:14.965
-(music stops)
-Whoo!

00:01:15.049 --> 00:01:17.259
I have one eye but all my original teeth.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.303
Would you like to count them? Ah...

00:01:19.386 --> 00:01:20.721
No, thank you.

00:01:21.722 --> 00:01:24.683
And this must be Nectarine.

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.519
-Um... Peaches.
-Semantics, my dear.

00:01:27.603 --> 00:01:28.938
I am deeply honored.

00:01:29.563 --> 00:01:32.775
Sweet eye patch. Very gangsta.

00:01:32.858 --> 00:01:33.984
Thank you.

00:01:34.068 --> 00:01:36.028
-I like this kid.
-MANNY: Buck.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.280
-Whoa!
-What are you doing here?

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.782
Well, I... What?

00:01:40.532 --> 00:01:41.700
I'm trying!

00:01:41.784 --> 00:01:44.203
But how do you tell someone
they're doomed?

00:01:44.912 --> 00:01:46.789
He's stumped. (laughs)

00:01:46.872 --> 00:01:47.998
We're not doomed, Buck.

00:01:48.082 --> 00:01:50.626
It was just a meteor shower,
and the show's over.

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:51.710
Ahh!

00:01:51.794 --> 00:01:53.170
Oh, quite the contrary, old chap.

00:01:53.253 --> 00:01:55.464
It's just beginning.

00:01:55.547 --> 00:01:58.550
You see, I found a prophecy.

00:01:59.468 --> 00:02:01.095
(dramatic drumming)

00:02:04.556 --> 00:02:05.724
Do you mind?

00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:09.645
Boy, he really sucks the fun
out of everything. Doesn't he?

00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:10.813
Fun sucker!

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.232
I read this tablet front to back.

00:02:13.315 --> 00:02:16.068
And the story it tells is very disturbing.

00:02:16.151 --> 00:02:18.487
Every hundred million years or so,

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.823
the world gets a cosmic cleansing.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:22.199
Before the dinosaurs,

00:02:22.282 --> 00:02:25.327
there were these horseshoe
crab-looking thingies.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.662
Ugh! Yuck.

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:28.580
Then, at the bottom of this mountain range,

00:02:28.664 --> 00:02:30.040
an asteroid hit.

00:02:30.124 --> 00:02:32.376
Boom! Bye-bye.

00:02:32.459 --> 00:02:35.671
Next, dinosaurs, mountain range, asteroid.

00:02:35.754 --> 00:02:37.172
Boom! Bye-bye.

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:39.508
And coming up next, mammals.

00:02:39.591 --> 00:02:41.593
Mountain range, asteroid, boom!

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:45.097
Bye-bye.

00:02:45.681 --> 00:02:48.392
-(giggles) Stupid mammals.
-That's us.

00:02:48.475 --> 00:02:49.476
(gasps)

00:02:49.852 --> 00:02:50.936
Mmm.

00:02:51.812 --> 00:02:53.856
Yep, and there she is.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:57.860
The mother of all asteroids
screaming towards us.

00:02:57.943 --> 00:03:00.529
Even going underground
won't save us this time.

00:03:00.612 --> 00:03:03.032
Hey, that wasn't there before.

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:05.117
And look what it's doing to the sky.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.536
No worries. Because I've got a plan.

00:03:07.619 --> 00:03:10.164
Really? To stop an asteroid?

00:03:10.706 --> 00:03:12.750
Look, the last two asteroids

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:14.918
have pummeled the earth in the same spot.

00:03:15.002 --> 00:03:17.046
And it's about to happen again.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:18.589
We've got to go there

00:03:18.672 --> 00:03:20.466
and see what's attracting the asteroid.

00:03:20.883 --> 00:03:22.551
Once we know why it's coming,

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:24.928
we can figure out
how to send it somewhere else.

00:03:25.012 --> 00:03:26.555
That plan is so dumb,

00:03:26.638 --> 00:03:28.974
I wish it had a face so I could smack it.

00:03:29.058 --> 00:03:30.225
Let me get this straight.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.811
Instead of running away from
a deadly asteroid,

00:03:32.895 --> 00:03:35.147
you want us to run directly towards it?

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.275
I know it sounds suboptimal,
but the good news is

00:03:38.358 --> 00:03:40.652
it'll kill us no matter where we went.

00:03:40.736 --> 00:03:42.446
Well, that's reassuring.

00:03:42.529 --> 00:03:44.907
Okay, but even if we get to the crash site

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.450
how are we supposed to change

00:03:46.533 --> 00:03:48.994
what is literally written in stone?

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:51.288
Ah, my cynical friend.

00:03:51.371 --> 00:03:53.415
The dinos were wiped off
the face of the Earth,

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.292
but some escaped.

00:03:55.375 --> 00:03:58.295
They changed their fate
and we can change ours, too.

00:03:58.378 --> 00:04:00.255
Who's with me?

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:01.715
(crickets chirping)

00:04:03.675 --> 00:04:05.636
So, what do you think?

00:04:05.719 --> 00:04:07.930
Honestly, I'm worried the weasel's right.

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:10.140
(in high-pitched voice) No!
don't listen to the weasel.

00:04:10.224 --> 00:04:12.684
He's a raving loon!

00:04:13.894 --> 00:04:16.605
(laughs) Sorry. I just
love playing devil's advocate.

00:04:16.688 --> 00:04:19.024
And looking fabulous!

00:04:20.692 --> 00:04:23.278
Well, Buck has saved our lives before, right?

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:25.322
But what if he can't this time?

00:04:25.405 --> 00:04:27.032
I don't know what to believe.

00:04:27.116 --> 00:04:31.036
But I'm afraid our lives will be over
before they begin.

00:04:33.122 --> 00:04:34.414
(chiseling)

00:04:35.457 --> 00:04:36.667
Okay.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.710
I guess we're in.

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:41.505
Crash and Eddie reporting for duty.

00:04:41.588 --> 00:04:42.965
(laughs) Doody.

00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:44.133
(both laughing)

00:04:44.216 --> 00:04:46.969
Excellent! And dirty word processed.

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:48.512
Now, we better get on the road

00:04:48.595 --> 00:04:50.139
because time till impact is roughly...

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:53.475
2 days, 4 hours, 1 minute and 16 seconds.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.310
15 seconds, 14 seconds...

00:04:55.894 --> 00:04:57.062
I think we get it.

00:04:57.479 --> 00:04:58.897
I think we're all gonna get it.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.825
Whoo! We look so cool.

00:05:09.908 --> 00:05:10.909
Whoa!

00:05:11.827 --> 00:05:13.453
(chuckling)

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:15.914
(coughing)

00:05:15.998 --> 00:05:18.083
Ugh. What is this stuff?

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:19.168
(screaming)

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:21.920
-(exhales)
-(groans)

